# Keyboard Switcher

A simple Windows desktop application built with Python and PySide6.

## What It Does

Keyboard Switcher monitors the active application and assigns a keyboard language to each configured profile.

Example:

```text
VS Code  → English
Opera    → Persian
When the active application changes, the application detects the process and identifies the corresponding profile.
Architecture
PySide6 UI
    ↓
Profile A / Profile B
    ↓
WindowMonitor
    ↓
Windows API + psutil
    ↓
Active Application
Technologies
- Python
- PySide6
- psutil
- pywin32
- PyInstaller
Project Structure
keyboard_switcher/
├── keyboard_switcher.py
├── main.py
├── main_window.py
├── run.py
├── requirements.txt
└── README.md
Development
Create and activate a virtual environment:
python -m venv venv
venv\Scripts\activate
Install dependencies:
pip install -r requirements.txt
Run the application:
python run.py
Build Windows Executable
Install PyInstaller:
pip install pyinstaller
Build:
pyinstaller --onefile --windowed --name KeyboardSwitcher run.py
The executable will be created at:
dist/KeyboardSwitcher.exe
Current Status
Implemented:
- PySide6 desktop UI
- Application selection
- Profile A and Profile B
- Keyboard language selection
- Active application monitoring
